  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1002 PM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nThe long term period will begin with lingering rainfall from an\naforementioned upper level trough and subsequent front that shifts\neastward over the area this weekend. Rain chances should subside from\nwest to east Sunday evening. This will be short-lived as low pressure\nresides over the southeast U.S., bringing daily shower/thunderstorm\nchances through mid week. Have continued with blended guidance for\nnow, keeping low to medium PoPs each afternoon due to disagreement in\nthe exact placement of the low within ensembles. Throughout the long\nterm, a gradual warm up is forecast with highs reaching the upper 80s\nto around 90 degrees by mid week. These temperatures will be\ndependent on potential cloud cover (or lack thereof) over the area.\nIf PoPs and coexisting cloud cover trend down as we approach next\nweek, highs will likely be a bit warmer than currently forecast.\nHowever, no heat products are on the horizon at this time.",
